<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">French Directory</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1795">1795</a>–<a href="/years/1799">1799</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Directoire</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The French Directory was the five-member executive that governed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-first-republic">French First Republic</a> from November 1795 to November 1799 under the Constitution of the Year III. It faced financial crisis, corruption and repeated coups against royalists and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacobin-club">Jacobins</a>, while its armies, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a>'s in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, created sister republics across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Bonaparte overthrew it in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coup-of-18-brumaire">Coup of 18 Brumaire</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Frederick William I created the General <b>Directory</b> in 1723 to run finance, war and the royal domains and recruited officials trained in cameralist administration, while the provincial estates kept their forms but lost most of their power.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-prussia">Kingdom of Prussia · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In early 1798 the <b>French Directory</b> sent armies into the Confederacy; Vaud proclaimed itself free, and after the defeat of Bernese forces at the Battle of Grauholz on 5 March 1798, Bern surrendered and the old order collapsed.</blockquote><a href="/empire/old-swiss-confederacy">Old Swiss Confederacy · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1796 Józef Wybicki, a leading moderate émigré politician, proposed Polish Legions within the French Revolutionary Army and persuaded General Jan Henryk Dąbrowski, a hero of the 1794 Kościuszko Uprising, to put the plan to the <b>French Directory</b>.</blockquote><a href="/songs/poland-is-not-yet-lost">Poland Is Not Yet Lost</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Directory</b> governed from 1795 amid corruption and coups.</blockquote><a href="/state/french-first-republic">French First Republic</a></li></ul></section>
